    "title": "Some Megyn Kelly callers push back on her coverage of the Cornell sexual assault case: \"I did stop listening to Megyn\" - NewsBreak",
    "text": "6 hours ago A woman known publicly as Jane Doe filed a lawsuit in September alleging that multiple men had raped her in a Cornell University fraternity house nearly two years prior. The case prompted outrage from right-wing media figures including Megyn Kelly, who said that the men were “being lynched in the media.\" Kelly has also said that Doe was “not the most attractive gal,” that she had possibly “liked the feeling of being sexy and desired and wanted,” and that it was “more comfortable for a young woman” to accuse men of rape than to admit she had “multiple threesomes with different men on one night.” Read full article",
